# Build context for deployments/Dockerfile (context = backend/).
#
# That Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the Go image build ships
# the entire ML workspace and the local caches to the daemon — close to a
# gigabyte, none of it needed to compile a Go binary.

# The ML workspace is a separate service with its own Dockerfile and its own
# build context (deployments/docker-compose.yml -> classifier). The Go image
# must never carry the Python virtualenv or the trained checkpoints.
ml/

# Local build caches and outputs (see .gitignore).
tmp/
bin/
dist/
.tmp/
*.test
*.out
coverage.html

# VCS and tooling
.git/
.github/
.cursor/
.cursor-plugin/
.air.toml

# Environment — never bake local secrets into an image layer.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Docs and repo furniture. Migrations are copied explicitly by the Dockerfile,
# so nothing here is needed at build time.
*.md
!README.md
docs/
postman/
LICENSE

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
